  "articleBody": "Drywall remodeling requires more precision than new construction because you are blending new materials with existing walls. Watch out for these common errors.\n\n- Patching over active moisture: Sealing drywall over damp wall cavities traps moisture and invites mold. Fix plumbing leaks and dry cavities fully before closing walls.\n- Leaving wet insulation behind: Putting new drywall against damp insulation ruins the new board. Always remove and replace compromised cavity insulation.\n- Mismatching sheet thickness: Using half-inch drywall against older 5/8-inch panels creates an uneven ridge that compound cannot hide. Match panel depths accurately.\n- Neglecting dust control: Demolition and sanding create fine dust that travels through heating ducts. Avoid this by insisting on plastic containment and floor masking.\n- Painting over uncured compound: Putting paint on damp mud causes bubbling, poor adhesion, and uneven sheen. Wait until joint compound is completely dry.\n\nHow to Compare Your Options\nWhen reviewing contractor quotes, check whether each quote covers demo, behind-the-wall checks, texture matching, and final primer.\n\nNeed drywall remodeling or repairs done right the first time? Call Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to review your remodel.",
